WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.589
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:07.860
First days of school are hard.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.560
I get it, I've been there.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.170
But my first in middle
school was different.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.519
I was sitting on my desk,
feeling like an outsider at a new school,

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:18.980
when I heard someone rush towards me.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.190
Hey, he said.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.700
We're missing one for table tennis.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:22.849
In Chinese it's ping pong.

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:24.699
So you in?

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:27.370
I ended up being surprised.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.130
I don't know how to play ping pong.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.060
It's okay, he said, we'll teach you.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.310
So he dragged me to a game with he and
his friends, boys and girls, and

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.340
we had a really good time.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.040
Now, full disclosure,
I still suck at ping pong.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.250
But I remember the feeling of
warmth of feeling included,

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.250
welcomed into that new community.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.220
The game brought me in.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.660
Four years ago, another friend of mine
dragged me to another game with him.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.830
It was at an old sports stadium
three hours away from Shanghai, and

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.940
it was pouring rain that day.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.370
Come on, I said to him,
nobody is going to travel three

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:16.300
hours in this horrifying rain to
watch people play video games.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.003
Plus, it's going to be awkward,

00:01:20.003 --> 00:01:22.530
I'm definitely going to
be the only girl there.

00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:30.175
Well, three hours later,
I was sitting at the stadium,

00:01:30.175 --> 00:01:37.717
soaking wet and surprised to find
myself surrounded by over 10,000 fans.

00:01:37.717 --> 00:01:44.510
They were young, they were excited,
their faces were painted 18 colors.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:50.630
And I looked out to the crowd,
I was definitely not the only girl there.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.740
In fact,
almost half of the audience was female.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.730
When the game started, it was like
someone lit a fire in the stadium.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:03.470
A dragon threw across the screen, and the
crowd broke into roaring waves of cheer.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.110
I looked around at the people
high-fiving around me,

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:10.550
some were older, most were younger,
some were men, some were women.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:17.400
And I felt well, the game, the video
game is bringing people together.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.308
And that excited me.

00:02:18.308 --> 00:02:22.426
For the following three years I co
founded an e-sports company in China,

00:02:22.426 --> 00:02:25.310
aiming to create
experiences just like this.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:28.560
To connect people through e-sports and
gaming.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.700
Now, fast-forward a couple years,
last summer I moved to the US.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:37.480
Now, I had heard about the difference
between the Eastern game culture and

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.840
the Western game culture.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.184
Namely, here,
it's a little bit more boy-centric.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.620
So I wanted to check it out myself.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:51.435
I drove up north to Oakland Esports Arena,
to a game of Fortnite.

00:02:51.435 --> 00:02:55.120
Fortnite is the massively
popular game here.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.940
And it's one of the most
gender balanced game here.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:01.618
It has over 46% of its player base female.

00:03:01.618 --> 00:03:05.585
I wanted to find a few female gamers and
ask them about their experience.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:09.433
When I got there, well,
this is not a 10,000 people arena,

00:03:09.433 --> 00:03:13.299
and there were no dragons or
anything, but it was still very cool.

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:16.950
It was a cool hip arena with
state of art computers.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:21.330
When I walked in the players and the fans
were glued to the screen immersed in their

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.430
game, and behind them was this big
screen showing what was going on.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.850
They didn't notice me when I walked in.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:29.714
But I noticed something.

00:03:29.714 --> 00:03:36.660
I was the only female there.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.570
And this is not a stand alone incident.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:45.000
I've heard women on podcasts and articles
talking about experiences similar to mine.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.620
Finding themselves to be one of
the very few females at Esports events.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:55.570
But wait a minute, if the stats
are correct, the percentage of

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:59.770
female gamers here in the US, is actually
quite comparable to that in China.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:03.440
In both countries,
almost half of the gamer base are female.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.180
Then where are the US female gamers?

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.000
Maybe they just don't like offline events.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.980
But then I realized,
it's not just offline.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:20.840
The female gamers here are not
showing up to offline events.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.640
And they're invisible online too.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.970
My friend Claire tells
me about her experience.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.500
Claire is an excellent Overwatch player.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.020
She's been playing the game
since it launched.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:40.789
And she tells me, that when she
plays Overwatch, She mutes her mic.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:43.999
Why do you mute your mic?

00:04:43.999 --> 00:04:45.247
I asked her.

00:04:45.247 --> 00:04:49.556
Well, she said, because I don't
want them to find out I'm a woman.

00:04:49.556 --> 00:04:53.002
What would happen if they
find out you're a woman?

00:04:53.002 --> 00:04:54.566
What would they do to you?

00:04:54.566 --> 00:04:59.790
For one thing, she said,
they would not invite me to the next game.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:06.040
On the other hand, there is also
that awkward private messages.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.340
Hey, how are you?

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.310
What are you doing?

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:10.160
What are you wearing?

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.100
Come on, I don't want any of that.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.257
I just want to play my game.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:24.170
There is an underlined assumption here
about the motivation of a female gamer.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.980
Namely, if you can't
proof your authenticity,

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:32.390
if you can prove your gaming skills and
your love of gaming by beating every

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:37.010
single person out there that challenges,
then you don't really like gaming.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.120
You're just doing it
to get guys attention.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.760
Well, this reminds me of an old joke.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.798
Which says, women go to colleges just to

00:05:50.798 --> 00:05:55.580
get husbands, just to get Mrs degree.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:03.130
Now, that joke is over half a century old,
but we're here in 2020 and gaming is new.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:07.210
It's no longer that small niche
industry in the 60s and 70s.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:11.100
It's now a giant industry
overtaking the entertainment forum.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.740
The global gaming
industry is $120 billion.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.579
It's bigger than the global movie box
office and the music industry combined.

00:06:18.579 --> 00:06:22.828
2.5 billion people around
the world are gamers.

00:06:22.828 --> 00:06:27.680
So it's now a big community,
got a big voice.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.802
And what kind of messages
are we saying with this voice?

00:06:34.516 --> 00:06:40.852
Then I realized there's also a second
layer of the issue, a less noticeable one.

00:06:40.852 --> 00:06:44.971
In 2015,
there was this incident called GamerGate,

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:50.770
in which online trolls attacked female
video game producers with rape threats and

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:54.990
death threats,
demanding them to get out of the industry.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:01.490
Brianna Wu, a female video game producer,
right at the center of GamerGate

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:06.780
reflected on her experience recently
in her Op-Ed on New York Times.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.361
She said, I wish I could tell
you things have gone better

00:07:11.361 --> 00:07:15.765
five years since the GamerGate,
but they haven't.

00:07:15.765 --> 00:07:20.928
She said, we built worlds of fantasy for
men, by men.

00:07:20.928 --> 00:07:26.840
For men, by men.

00:07:32.473 --> 00:07:36.470
Now, the issue we're seeing here
in video games, it's not fresh.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.290
We've seen it before.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:41.380
We've seen it in Hollywood,
we've seen it in traditional sports,

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.070
we've seen it right
here in Silicon Valley.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:49.300
But we have a unique window
of opportunity here.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:54.610
The gaming industry, despite its rapid
growth is still growing, it's still small.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.080
It will grow bigger.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.280
It's growing to take even more
dominant part of our social life, and

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.100
not just our generation,
but generations to come.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.630
We gotta do something here.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:07.210
What can we do?

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:12.270
Well, I think three things to be done.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:20.230
One, if you're a female gamer,

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:25.390
unmute your mic,
speak up because you deserve to be heard.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:31.965
If you are a male gamer,
actually mute your mic.

00:08:31.965 --> 00:08:36.190
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Try this for a change.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:40.760
When you go home tonight, sign on to
your favorite game and create a new ID,

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.840
a female ID, with a female name,

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:48.010
and see what happens to you,
and notice how you feel.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:50.330
What you would like to be changed.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.670
Two, if you're running a game company,
which I know some of you may go on to do,

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:02.015
think about who you're bringing
on to your creative staff.

00:09:02.015 --> 00:09:04.635
Think about who you have
on your production team.

00:09:04.635 --> 00:09:09.316
Because the digital world,
just like our real world,

00:09:09.316 --> 00:09:14.216
should be created for
everyone by everyone, isn't it?

00:09:16.598 --> 00:09:20.339
Three, if you are none of the above, well,

00:09:20.339 --> 00:09:25.195
whatever your form of game play is,
Pokemon Go, Jenga,

00:09:25.195 --> 00:09:31.180
Texas Hold'em, bring someone in,
invite someone, bring them in.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:38.220
When I moved here last summer I brought
my tickets with me, a six year old and

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:38.810
a two year old.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.579
I remember feeling very nervous
taking them to their first play date.

00:09:46.405 --> 00:09:47.140
Would they make friends?

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.930
Would they be accepted?

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:54.670
because when they moved here,
they didn't speak a lick of English.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:57.870
Will they be included?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.696
Or would they be like their mother,
when I was their age,

00:10:03.696 --> 00:10:07.409
where they just sit
silently in the corner?

00:10:07.409 --> 00:10:10.648
When we got there the party
had already started,

00:10:10.648 --> 00:10:15.077
the kids had laid out toys on the floor,
blocks, Lego and switch.

00:10:15.077 --> 00:10:19.762
My kids jumped with joy and
immediately they rushed in, and

00:10:19.762 --> 00:10:24.460
the children started playing the games,
brought them in.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:27.134
Thank you.

00:10:27.134 --> 00:10:28.775
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:10:28.775 --> 00:10:34.322
[MUSIC]

